  "direction": "Low-rank adaptation at tiny scale: pretrain a small character-level transformer on one synthetic sequence task (e.g. copying or sorting digits), then adapt it to a related task (reversal, or sorting in the other order) with full fine-tuning, LoRA at ranks 1, 2, 4 and 8, and training only the last layer. Measure adaptation accuracy, number of trained parameters, and forgetting of the pretraining task.",
